Build location sets where the build happens.

**Local** does everything on this machine, reading the app schema from its own database. **Remote** fetches the app schema (views, pages, tables, plugins) from another server instead.

Use Remote when this machine is just for building (e.g. a Mac for the Xcode toolchain), not your live server.

**Setup:**
1. Generate an API key for an admin user on your live server.
2. Remote server URL: `https://<live-server>` (just the base URL)
3. Remote API key: that key.

Both fields are required when Build location is set to Remote.
